      "message": "That a specific build exits successfully doesn\u0027t mean that it\u0027s a correct build, or covers anything more than a fraction of the possible actions. There\u0027s both a bug reference and comments around why some of them are necessary. Others may fail relatively quietly unless you\u0027re looking for them. And others are only required for certain cases: rbe 🙂, goma (which should be able to be removed), ccache (which we don\u0027t care about too much, but still get bugs), dist builds (on specific error cases... [1]), host ASAN, etc. And some of them I just couldn\u0027t prove whether they were used or not -- either way, we should make both systems behave the same way.\n\n1: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/make/core/Makefile;drc\u003dad4dae71cf5daf8c93ce0850fe198692d8223396;l\u003d2515",
